1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,535
CHAPTER 2 — TWO STEVES, ONE PAYCHECK

2
00:00:03,885 --> 00:00:10,346
In 1974, Jobs joined Atari, the hottest video game company around, as a technician.

3
00:00:10,546 --> 00:00:18,700
He had a theory: since he ate almost only fruit, he didn't need to shower often. His coworkers did not agree.

4
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:30,054
Atari moved him to the night shift. Its founder, Nolan Bushnell, later said he got a bonus out of it: Wozniak came in at night to help him. Two Steves for the price of one.

5
00:00:30,254 --> 00:00:38,177
Atari asked Jobs for a game using very few chips: Breakout. Wozniak designed it in four nights, barely sleeping.

6
00:00:38,377 --> 00:00:46,839
Jobs told him they had been paid 700 dollars, and gave him half. According to Wozniak, the real bonus was around 5,000.

7
00:00:47,789 --> 00:00:56,558
He found out about ten years later, reading a book. He said he cried. And that if Jobs had just asked for the money, he would have given it to him.
